<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-navy dark:text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="gold-underline w-16 mt-2 mb-6"></div>
  <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-sm">
    <p><strong>What we collect.</strong> When you register we collect your name, email address, and the learning records you create (lesson progress, quiz attempts, assignment submissions, grades, certificates). Contact-form messages are stored so we can reply.</p>
    <p><strong>How we use it.</strong> Your information is used to operate the academy: delivering courses, tracking your progress, issuing certificates, and communicating with you about your studies. We do not sell personal data.</p>
    <p><strong>Who can see it.</strong> Your learning records are visible to you and to academy staff (teachers and administrators) who need them to teach and support you. Public certificate verification shows only the information needed to authenticate a certificate.</p>
    <p><strong>Security.</strong> Passwords are stored as salted hashes. Access to records is restricted by role, and important administrative actions are logged.</p>
    <p><strong>Your rights.</strong> You may update your profile at any time and request correction or deletion of your personal data by contacting the academy.</p>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">This is a plain-language summary for Phase 1. Have it reviewed by a qualified professional before relying on it for legal compliance.</p>
  </div>
</div>
